{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792366618,"nonce":"5jnjqivx5omzhAFDpJkxgfJjT5A=","title":"Browser load: the program, its libraries and the host module download one after another, and the module is rewritten after the last byte","message":"worker.js fetched the program to the end, then each library in turn, and ran only then. ashui's dashboard (23 MB wasm, 5.9 MB brotli, plus four libraries and the 1.9 MB host module) takes minutes on a slow link, and about 1.1 s of module rewriting and linking starts only after the last byte arrives.\n\nMeasured with a throttled server (shared bandwidth, one round trip per response, brotli, cold cache), time until the worker starts the program:\n- 10 Mbit, 80 ms: 8.55 s sequential, 7.65 s with every download started together; the wire is 8.5 MB, so the floor is 6.8 s.\n- 50 Mbit, 40 ms: 2.13 s against 1.80 s; the app reports ready at 5.7 s against 5.4 s.\n\nDone: the host module, the program and the libraries are requested together, and each step is stamped in the page's meta lines.\n\nLeft:\n- Rewrite and link the program module while the libraries still download: `run` takes the whole program's bytes, so it needs a prepare step that returns a handle. Worth at most the 1.1 s.\n- Bytes: the program is most of the wire. A smaller module (names stripped, dead code removed) and brotli at its top quality save more than any ordering.","files":null}]}